Android beta 122 as a preview (roadmap 214): the headset keeper after its
first run on a device. Android only: the code is under Q_OS_ANDROID, no
iOS build is made and build 216 stays the newest on TestFlight. The
user's word of 2026-11-26, about 08:20 ("push"), to mending 214 and pushing it
for their own phone; to everyone only on their word after the try.
On the OnePlus Open with the Jabra Evolve2 65, Audio output Auto, media
audio off:
1. Some minutes of normal use. If the link drops by itself again, the
   sound has to be back in the headset within a few seconds (the log:
   "headset link down for ...", perhaps "Android gave the headset no
   route this time", then "headset link back after ...").
2. The headset switched off while connected: the sound to the phone
   ("Android lists no Bluetooth headset any more"); switched on again:
   back in the headset within about five seconds of Android listing it.
3. A phone call with the app in the background, and one with it in front:
   "a phone call (audio mode 2): the headset's route left alone", and the
   headset back after "the phone call has ended".
4. To the background and back with the headset playing: no interruption
   at the return.
5. What beta 121 did well still holds: receive at once after PTT, the
   link mended in the background in about three seconds.
Then Bluetooth media and back to Auto, and the same with media audio on.
